# No em dashes

Do not use the em dash character (`—`) or the pattern ` — ` anywhere in this project: UI copy, content modules, metadata titles, comments that surface in docs, or generated text.

## Prefer instead

- Comma or period for asides: `Migration, rebuild, operations.`
- Colon for labels: `Email: hello@denwebs.com`
- Section indexes with a period: `01. Work` (never `01 — Work`)
- Title separators with a pipe: `Audits | Denwebs` (never `Audits — Denwebs`)
- Hyphen or en dash only for numeric ranges if needed: `1-3 months`, `$50k-250k`

## Also avoid

- HTML entities `&mdash;` / `&#8212;`
- Fake em dashes made of double hyphens (` -- `) in user-facing copy
- Eyebrow/`::before` ornaments that look like a dash before labels (no `— Contact` look)

When editing existing strings that still contain `—`, rewrite them to one of the forms above.
